WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.259
Web and API input should be validated on the server before business logic acts on it.

00:00:07.259 --> 00:00:14.518
Request bodies, path parameters, query parameters, headers, cookies, form fields, and file metadata all need expectations.

00:00:14.518 --> 00:00:21.362
Frameworks can help, but framework defaults are not the same as a complete validation design.

00:00:21.362 --> 00:00:26.961
The application should define what each endpoint accepts and what it rejects.

00:00:26.961 --> 00:00:31.731
Flask applications often require explicit request parsing and validation choices.

00:00:31.731 --> 00:00:37.746
Django provides forms, model forms, serializers in common API stacks, and validation hooks.

00:00:37.746 --> 00:00:42.931
FastAPI commonly uses Pydantic models for request bodies and typed parameters.

00:00:42.931 --> 00:00:53.093
Each framework offers tools, but the developer is still responsible for applying them consistently and enforcing business rules that the framework cannot infer.

00:00:53.093 --> 00:00:55.789
File metadata deserves special attention.

00:00:55.789 --> 00:01:03.048
A filename, extension, content type, declared size, and form field may all be user-controlled or misleading.

00:01:03.048 --> 00:01:12.796
A server should validate file size, expected type, allowed use, storage location, and how the file will later be served or processed.

00:01:12.796 --> 00:01:18.810
Validation should not depend on the client telling the truth about the upload.

00:01:18.810 --> 00:01:23.580
Validation error messages should be useful without revealing unnecessary internals.

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:30.839
A response can say that a field is required, out of range, malformed, or not allowed.

00:01:30.839 --> 00:01:40.587
It should not expose stack traces, secret values, database structure, parser internals, or implementation details that do not help a legitimate user.

00:01:40.587 --> 00:01:47.431
Good API validation gives clear feedback while keeping sensitive information out of responses and logs.
